# setup.py's package_data was never declared, so a real (non-editable)
# install has only ever picked up FreeBodyEngine's *.py files -
# find_packages() only discovers Python packages, nothing about data
# files. Every dev/test install of this repo has been `pip install -e .`
# (see ~/.venvs/dev's own editable install), which just points at the
# source tree directly and never goes through packaging at all - so this
# gap was invisible until phonon's Pi deploy pipeline did the first-ever
# real `pip install` of this package and immediately hit a missing
# engine_assets/shader/*.fbvert file at runtime.
#
# Includes everything under FreeBodyEngine/ (shaders, fonts, other
# engine_assets, desktop lib/ DLLs) rather than trying to enumerate every
# asset type by extension - this is a private, all-in-one engine package,
# not something with an installed footprint worth trimming, and every
# missing-file bug this could still leave is strictly worse than the
# install being a bit larger than strictly necessary.
recursive-include FreeBodyEngine *
global-exclude *.pyc
global-exclude __pycache__
